            <ArticleTitle>[Gluteal compartment syndrome after intramuscular gluteal injection].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>366-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Complications after i.m. injection are rare. Only few cases need emergency operative treatment. This case report shows the exclusive situation of a gluteal compartment syndrome caused by a hematoma. Clinical findings showed signs of nerve compression with sciatic pain. Only immediate surgical treatment prevented persistent nerve or muscle tissue damage.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
